   "text": {
    "L1": "Perimeter is the total length around a shape's boundary.",
    "L2": "A common mistake is to add the length and breadth only once. That gives just one length and one breadth.",
    "L3": "A rectangle has two lengths and two breadths, so perimeter is 2 times length plus breadth.",
    "L4": "For 45 centimetres by 30 centimetres, the perimeter is 2 times 75, or 150 centimetres.",
    "L5": "A square has four equal sides, so its perimeter is 4 times its side. On a grid, count unit lengths along the edge, not squares.",
    "L6": "Now find the perimeter of a rectangle that is 8 centimetres by 5 centimetres."
   },
   "narration": {
